                                                "sense_id": "51a64f61-23ab-3af7-b5da-62d75587ecd2",
                                                "text": "Mucocutaneous habronemiasis became much less common following widespread use of oral avermectin and anthelmintic compounds that kill the gastric nematodes whose larvae cause this cutaneous lesion."
